From: Brian Cain <brian.cain@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 15:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gallium: fix tgsi_opcode_info opcode bitfield width on
 hexagon

Same class of issue as the pipe_transfer::usage fix: 'enum tgsi_opcode'
currently fits in 8 bits on every enumerator, so the Hexagon ABI (which
picks the smallest unsigned integer type that fits all enumerators for
a plain enum) uses an 8-bit underlying type for it. The 10-bit
'opcode' bitfield is then wider than its own declared type, which
Clang rejects:

  error: width of bit-field 'opcode' (10 bits) exceeds the width of
  its type (8 bits)

Use a plain unsigned bitfield instead, as already done for the
neighboring fields in this struct.

Signed-off-by: Brian Cain <brian.cain@gmail.com>
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_info.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_info.h b/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_info.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_info.h
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_info.h
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@
    unsigned pre_dedent:1;
    unsigned post_indent:1;
    enum tgsi_output_mode output_mode:4;
-   enum tgsi_opcode opcode:10;
+   unsigned opcode:10;              /**< TGSI_OPCODE_x */
 };

 const struct tgsi_opcode_info *
